[{:seon.task/name "the-fork-is-upstream-plus-what-seon-needs"
  :seon.task/plan "The owner's ruling (docs/decisions.md, 2026-11-10; docs/forks.md#following-upstream): Datahike is rebuilt as upstream's head with only what Seon needs applied on top, theirs taken wherever it is almost as good. What exists: our fork is 274 commits and about 10,400 added source lines over the merge base `85c40aee` (2026-07-14), upstream 186 commits ahead; only 16 of ours are the Jolt port; about 51 are in themes nothing in Seon calls (host capabilities, the Proximum integration, query-cache identity and single flight); the writer (26) and the versioning and collection work overlap what upstream has since redesigned. A slice-by-slice merge met 140 conflict blocks in its third slice alone. A first overlay exists in the fork session's scratch clone (branch `jolt/overlay-on-upstream`, 9 commits, 285 source lines, never compiled, not reviewed): the Jolt port in part, the schema sets, the store-fixed keys, `datoms-diff` as a thin function over upstream's sorted-set `diff`, `after-fork!`. Not carried yet, each Seon calls: the run-ahead writer; store-wide ids and ``:db/contentId``; `with-reads`; the commit graph with `merge-base` and `keep-commits`; values out of line; the unique `[a v]` one-descent seek. Our 52 query fixes are to be run against upstream's head first and carried only where a test of ours still fails there. Decided by the rule: upstream's background index build is left out on Jolt (its codec `boring` is Java classes); upstream's node cache by entry count is taken, with values out of line carried so nodes are near one size; maps and sets order by hash as upstream's do (stores indexing such values are erased); `deliver` is fixed in Jolt. The one design choice: the writer. Seon needs from it only apply without commit, commit the batch once, abandon; the shape to prove is Seon holding the applied value (a `d/with` chain) and the commit handing that value to upstream's `datahike.writing/commit!` with the head revision it expects, so the fork carries one small function and upstream's writer stays whole. It needs the sorted set's upstream functions on Jolt (task org.replikativ.persistent-sorted-set/upstreams-diff-and-bulk-build-are-on-jolt). What Seon changes with it is listed in the scratch report (16 call sites of `d/datoms-diff`, `:store-cache-bytes`). Done means: Seon's whole prove green on the overlay pin, the fork's difference from upstream stated in docs/forks.md by theme with its reason, each number that moved measured."
  :seon.task/kind :work
  :seon.task/proofs #{}}
]
